From 19005fb55300f0ad0bc1bd932878cfec472e40a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 03:52:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: a held mode that goes out alone keeps the HDR
 of the video

When the driver refuses the commit of a held change of mode together with
the HDR signalling of the video, the mode goes out alone with the next
commit and the output of the video after it (CHeldModeAnnouncement:
MODE_ALONE, then OUTPUT_AFTER). But SettleHDR() runs at the start of that
next frame: the request that carried the HDR change is finished and the
kernel still has the state before it, so the change was taken as refused
and the state went back to SDR. OUTPUT_AFTER then queued that again
(HDR_OUTPUT_METADATA 0): the video played in its mode without its HDR
signalling, while the log said that its output goes with the next commit.

The change was not refused: the commit that the driver refused carried it
together with the mode, and it is queued again after the mode. SettleHDR()
now leaves the state as it is while the mode of a held change goes out
alone (CHeldModeAnnouncement::Alone()). OUTPUT_AFTER queues the HDR
metadata of the video, the state before it moves to that request
(CHDRSignal::Requeued()), and the frame after that request settles it from
what the kernel has, as for any other change.

Host test: hdrsettle_test with a driver that refuses a change of mode and
of HDR_OUTPUT_METADATA in one commit and takes each alone. The video ends
in its mode with its HDR, and no refusal of the HDR is logged. Without this
change it ends with HDR_OUTPUT_METADATA 0.
---
 xbmc/windowing/gbm/ModeChangeHold.h |  5 +++++
 xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.cpp | 10 ++++++++++
 2 files changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/ModeChangeHold.h b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/ModeChangeHold.h
index c9294f7..fddb9b0 100644
--- a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/ModeChangeHold.h
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/ModeChangeHold.h
@@ -325,6 +325,11 @@ public:
     return Then::NOTHING;
   }
   Step Pending() const { return m_step; }
+  //! Hades: the mode of a held change goes out alone with the next commit (MODE_ALONE), and the
+  //! output of the video after it (OUTPUT_AFTER queues it again). What the output of the video
+  //! carried (its HDR signalling) is still to go out meanwhile: the refused commit did not carry
+  //! it, and that is no refusal of it.
+  bool Alone() const { return m_alone; }
 
 private:
   Step m_step = Step::NONE;
diff --git a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.cpp b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.cpp
index 5e7e2b2..3c8ab07 100644
--- a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.cpp
@@ -2632,6 +2632,16 @@ void CWinSystemGbm::SettleHDR()
 {
   if (!m_hdrBefore)
     return;
+#ifdef HAVE_DVBRIDGE
+  // The commit of a held change of mode with the output of the video was refused, and the mode
+  // goes out alone first (HeldModeChangeCommitted(): MODE_ALONE). The kernel has the HDR state
+  // before the change then, but the change is not refused: OUTPUT_AFTER queues it again after the
+  // mode. Settled now, the state would go back to the one before, and that is what OUTPUT_AFTER
+  // queued again: the video went on without its HDR signalling while the log said it goes with
+  // the next commit. It is settled once the request that carries it again is finished.
+  if (m_modeAnnounce.Alone())
+    return;
+#endif
   const auto drm = std::dynamic_pointer_cast<CDRMAtomic>(m_DRM);
   if (!drm)
     return;
-- 
